We start with a catalogue that maps SKUs to names.

my %catalogue = (
    "CF-100" => "Coffee Beans",
    "MG-200" => "Ceramic Mug",
    "BN-300" => "Beans",
);

then we take the SKUs and sort them. my @skus = sort keys !-1;
and we print every SKU and name.

foreach my $sku (@skus) {
    print "$sku: $catalogue{$sku}\n";
}

and count them. my $count = @skus;
finally we show the count. print "items: $count\n";
